Ji Won Yoon received her B.S. degree in Materials Science and Engineering from Korea University in 2016. She is currently a Ph.D. candidate in Materials Science and Engineering under the supervision of Prof. Jong-Heun Lee at the Functional Nanostructured Materials Laboratory, Korea University. Her research focuses on the design of MOF/oxide hybrid for photoelectrochemical water splitting.
Jae-Hyeok Kim received his B.S. degree in Materials Science and Engineering from Korea University in 2015. He is currently a Ph.D. candidate in Materials Science and Engineering under the supervision of Prof. Jong-Heun Lee at the Functional Nanostructured Materials Laboratory, Korea University. His research focuses on the design of various hybrids including oxides and MOFs for photoelectrochemical water splitting.
Changyeon Kim received his B.S. degree in the School of Advanced Materials Science and Engineering from Sungkyunkwan University, in 2016. He is currently a Ph.D. candidate in the Department of Materials Science and Engineering under the supervision of Prof. Ho Won Jang at the Oxide Nanostructures & Nanoelectronics Laboratory, Seoul National University. His research focuses on the design of various oxide nanomaterials and their application on solar water splitting and photoelectrochemical ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ reduction studies.
Ho Won Jang is an associate professor in the Department of Materials Science and Engineering, Seoul National University. He received his Ph.D. from the Department of Materials Science and Engineering of Pohang University of Science and Technology in 2004. His research interests include the synthesis of metal oxide thin films, low-dimensional materials, and halide perovskites, and the application of those materials to various devices including chemical sensors for electronic nose and tongue, photoelectrochemical water splitting cells, memristors, optoelectronics, smart windows, and nanophotonics.
Jong-Heun Lee joined the Department of Materials Science and Engineering at Korea University as an associate professor in 2003, where he has been a full professor since 2008. He received his B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees from Seoul National University in 1987, 1989, and 1993, respectively. He was a senior researcher at the Samsung Advanced Institute of Technology (1993–1999) and a research professor at Seoul National University (2000–2003). His current research interests are functional materials.
